# Recipe stage 2 (PLAN.md v2 section 6): one-factor sweeps at a 1M FP16 cache on cB = C12 (plain, chunk 4096: the
# decode-best split of stage 1) and K4 = C11 (pipelined 4096 / 16384: the prefill-best split). Code: dsv41-all tip 5e55c062
# (source /root/rnd/release/all/src-5e55c0627ece via WS_SRC, native sha256 823174af46fb). Harness recipe/bench3 (version 5 =
# bench2 + --ngram-draft). ONE window: round 1 here (one process per arm, C12 references first and last), round 2 (second
# processes of the arms that beat the reference, mirrored, plus conditional lines) appended to the requeue file, which the
# driver drains before the first optional line. Memory: py_memwatch (8 GiB floor, kills only its own PID) in a swap-0
# cgroup of 119G; pinned + resident <= 120 GB on every line (E3 sized for it); minavail = expected RSS + ~18-20 GiB.
# N-class arms are gated by greedy-token equality with the C12 references (tokens_sha256_12 per job).

# ---- round 1: one process per arm; C12 reference first (it also writes the heat file for C12-HR) and last
#@ est=12 timeout=1500 minavail=87
C12-R1 | BENCH_PYTHON=/root/rnd/release/all/aux/py_memwatch.sh MEMWATCH_PY=/root/rnd/release/recipe/bench3/py_mem.sh PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 MEMMAX=119G PYTORCH_ALLOC_CONF=backend:cudaMallocAsync PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=backend:cudaMallocAsync EXL3_PLACEMENT='0-11=cuda:0; 12-39=cuda:1 experts=cache; ram experts=all; disk experts=off' EXL3_MOE_HEAT_FILE=/root/rnd/release/recipe/stage2/heat/c12-r1.exl3moe | --modes h2h --scenarios full --chunk 4096 --cache-tokens 1048576 --max-output-size 32 --engram-drop --timeline 32 --expect-native-sha 823174af46fb
